2.1.evidence:
Article 29
(1) Regional Government may conduct cooperation in order to achieve the objectives of implementing protection for women and children victims of violence.
(2) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1) shall be conducted with:
a. Government;
b. Provincial government;
c. Other regency/city government; and
d. Non-governmental institutions.
(3) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (1), includes:
a. Exchange of data and information;
b. Rehabilitation of victims of acts of Violence;
c. Repatriation and social reintegration; and
d. Provision of evidence and witnesses and followed up in accordance with Laws and Regulations.
(4) Cooperation as referred to in paragraph (2) and paragraph (3), shall be conducted in the form of Joint Agreement.

